<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ica River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ica River flows from the Andes to the Pacific through the coastal desert of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, watering a valley around the city of Ica. Its oasis valley was a centre of the Paracas and Nazca cultures and later of the Ica culture, and it is now known for its vineyards and pisco. Water is scarce, and farming depends on irrigation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groundwater-depletion">groundwater</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ica-river.jpg" alt="Ica River" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfredobi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puente_en_la_cidad_de_ICA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
